==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|milk|y}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪlki/}}
* {{rhymes|ɪlki}}

The meaning "cowardly" was possibly coined by Graham Greene in the novel ''Brighton Rock'' (1938).

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# Resembling [[milk]] in [[color]] or [[consistency]].
# {{context|color science|informal|lang=en}} Of the [[black]] in an [[image]], appearing as dark [[gray]] rather than black.
# {{context|colloquial|lang=en}} [[cowardly|Cowardly]].

